sonar_slam_backend — a modified fork of slam_toolbox (LGPL-2.1)

This package is derived from SteveMacenski/slam_toolbox, foxy branch,
upstream commit 4786e90 ("backport #377 foxy (#477)", 2022-02-22), which
in turn bundles the Karto SDK (lib/karto_sdk). The back-end sources retain
the upstream LGPL-2.1 notice in LICENSE; the Karto SDK has its own LGPL-3.0
notice in lib/karto_sdk/LICENSE. Some retained upstream headers also carry
their original Creative Commons Public License notice. These component
licenses are separate and are not replaced by the package.xml summary.

Modified 2026 for a Ping360 mechanical-scanning-sonar SLAM system. The
package and its C++ namespace were renamed from slam_toolbox to
sonar_slam_backend; upstream features not used by that system (lifelong
and localization modes, async node, map merging, the RViz plugin, tests,
sample configs and launch files) were removed. Files whose logic changed:

  lib/karto_sdk/src/Mapper.cpp, lib/karto_sdk/include/karto_sdk/Mapper.h
      loop-closure decision layer: response thresholds set from the
      platform's measured match-response distribution; a position-jump
      gate (LoopMatchMaximumPositionJump) that rejects a loop candidate
      whose implied pose correction exceeds a scene-scaled bound; grid-
      index guards in the correlation search (out-of-range candidates
      score zero instead of throwing); failed matches degrade to zero
      response / maximal covariance instead of aborting.
  src/sonar_slam_backend_common.cpp, include/.../sonar_slam_backend_common.hpp
      per-scan exception isolation so one degenerate frame is skipped
      rather than terminating mapping; rollback of a half-registered scan.
  src/slam_mapper.cpp
      exposes the new loop-closure parameters.
  CMakeLists.txt, package.xml
      trimmed to the retained sources.

The modified files above describe implementation changes made for this
repository. Experimental rationale and parameter values are documented in
the accompanying manuscript and configuration files; this notice is not a
claim that the modified implementation is numerically identical to the
upstream package.

Release packaging (2026-10-09): the unused G2O CMake requirement and
commented-out solver plugin examples were removed. Ceres remains the solver.
The package manifest now declares nav2_map_server, used by the map export service.
